            "review_title": "Review at Phở Việt Nam - Hồ Tùng Mậu",
            "review_text": "Stephen K\nFrance67 contributions\n1\nAmazing, simply amazing\nDec 2025 • Solo\nPho Viet Nam have a number of locations dotted all over Ho Chi Minh City, I am currently eating at one of their locations at least 5 or 6 times a week. \n\nAfter reading so many BEST PHO in Saigon Reviews, from people who clearly have no idea of what they are talking about, and or, have only spent a brief time in this sprawling metropolis, l decided to give the subject a deeper dive.\n\nI have now visited over 100 different pho restaurants in HCMC, and Pho Viet Nam have consistently stayed in my favourite top 3. I highly recommend any of their pho restaurants as they hit the spot each and every time. \n\nEven after 5 months in Saigon, and eating pho every day, I still don't feel confident to claim that any one establishment is The Best. The very idea of best is too subjective, and what particular variety of pho is being evaluated? All of mine have been bowls of pho bo tei. This was the easiest way to afford each a level playing field.\n\nWhat I can tell you with a high degree of confidence is that a steaming bowl of pho bo tei from Pho Viet Nam will arrive at your table with a deep and aromatic broth, fresh made noodles, high quality thinly sliced beef and a generous array of accompaniments: crisp beansprouts, fresh sliced raw chillies, lime wedges and a mound of Asian herbs. You will also find a further assortment of options on your table that allow you to further customise your meal. My favourites are the pickled garlic, the minced chilli paste and the pickled shallots. \n\nYou will see that they have been awarded Michelin Selected status for a number of years, but not at all locations. Don't let that put you off, each of their restaurants push out the same high quality, excellent pho. \n\nI moved into a small apartment in Japan Town area of District 1, so this particular restaurants near the Bitexco Tower became my closest.\nRead more\nWritten December 3, 2025",
